From f31f91a412d95407c0ef20bc547462e8ba0d6122 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guy Lyons <guylyons2@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 03:09:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] macos-arm64: ray-traced reflections

Surfaces whose material has an environment map reflect; water keeps the
engine's own mirrored render. Per-triangle material tables (reflectivity,
tint, flat colour) travel with every mesh: reflectivity comes from
$envmaptint times the average of the material's mask ($envmapmask, base
alpha or normal-map alpha, read from the texture's smallest mip), the flat
colour from the face's lightmap average times the texture's reflectivity.
A short probe from just above the surface identifies each pixel's triangle;
one reflected ray (glossy by roughness) per pixel on an alternating
checkerboard takes the colour from the captured frame when the hit is on
screen and the flat colour otherwise. Reflections accumulate with their own
history, are blurred depth-aware, and are composited in a second additive
pass with a view-dependent falloff. The budget controller drops reflections
as its second tier. rt_reflections, rt_reflection_strength,
rt_reflection_roughness, rt_sky_color, rt_list_reflective; rt_debug 5/6.
